{"id":"534caa90954418aa3aea0ffbfd92a7fc5088a291","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-02937-z","title":"Efficient yet stable large perovskite solar modules made using surface treatment","site_name":"Buzzing","source":"www.nature.com","byline":null,"excerpt":"Non-uniformities in the layer of passivator molecules, which are used to fix defects and protect the surface of perovskite material in solar cells, can limit the durability of the resulting modules. Large modules treated instead with chemically stable lead carboxylate passivators were efficient, reliable and had a higher yield than did commercial silicon modules. Solar modules treated with lead carboxylate passed the standard test of photovoltaic reliability and had a high yield.","content_html":"<DIV class=\"page\" id=\"readability-page-1\"><div id=\"content\" data-container-type=\"article\" data-component=\"article-container\">\n            \n\n            \n\n            <article data-track-component=\"news\" lang=\"en\">\n                \n                <div>\n                    \n                        <div>\n    <header>\n        <div>\n            <ul data-test=\"article-identifier\">\n                \n                    <li data-test=\"article-category\"><span>RESEARCH BRIEFINGS</span></li>\n                    <li>\n                        <time datetime=\"2026-09-23\">23 September 2026</time>\n                    </li>\n                \n                \n            </ul>\n\n            \n\n            <div>\n                \n                <p>\n                    Non-uniformities in the layer of passivator molecules, which are used to fix defects and protect the surface of perovskite material in solar cells, can limit the durability of the resulting modules. Large modules treated instead with chemically stable lead carboxylate passivators were efficient, reliable and had a higher yield than did commercial silicon modules.\n                </p>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n        \n    </header>\n\n    \n    \n    \n        \n            \n    \n\n        \n    \n</div>\n                    \n\n                    \n\n                    \n                        \n                        <p>This is a summary of: <a href=\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-026-10994-7\" data-track=\"click\" data-label=\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-026-10994-7\" data-track-category=\"body text link\">Xu, D. <i>et al</i>. Lead carboxylates passivation for metre-scale perovskite solar modules. <i>Nature</i> <b>657</b>, 918–924 (2026)</a>.</p>\n                        \n                        \n                    \n                        <p><em>doi: https://doi.org/10.1038/d41586-026-02937-z</em></p><p>‘Expert opinion’ is published under a CC BY 4.0 licence.</p>\n\n                    <div aria-labelledby=\"Bib1\" id=\"references\"><h2 id=\"Bib1\">References</h2><div id=\"Bib1-content\" data-container-section=\"references\"><ol data-track-component=\"outbound reference\" data-track-context=\"references section\"><li data-counter=\"1.\"><p id=\"ref-CR1\">Green, M. A. <i>et al.</i> <i>Joule</i> <b>10</b>, 102494 (2026).</p><p><a data-track=\"click_references\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" data-track-label=\"10.1016/j.joule.2026.102494\" data-track-item_id=\"10.1016/j.joule.2026.102494\" data-track-value=\"article reference\" data-track-action=\"article reference\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.1016%2Fj.joule.2026.102494\" aria-label=\"Article reference 1\" data-doi=\"10.1016/j.joule.2026.102494\">Article</a>&#160;\n    <a data-track=\"click_references\" data-track-action=\"google scholar reference\" data-track-value=\"google scholar reference\" data-track-label=\"link\" data-track-item_id=\"link\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" aria-label=\"Google Scholar reference 1\" href=\"http://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?&title=&journal=Joule&doi=10.1016%2Fj.joule.2026.102494&volume=10&publication_year=2026&author=Green%2CM.%20A.\">\n                  