channel peptide nanofibrils","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p><span>Article</span> <span><time datetime=\"2026-09-23\">23 SEP 26</time></span></p>","sentences":[{"en":"Article 23 SEP 26","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<li>\n                        <a href=\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-026-11069-3\" data-track=\"select_article\" data-track-action=\"view latest magazine article\" data-track-index=\"2\">\n                            \n                                <img src=\"https://media.nature.com/w140h79/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41586-026-11069-3/MediaObjects/41586_2026_11069_Fig1_HTML.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">\n                            \n                            <p>Stacking-induced direct band gap in CVD-grown 1H MoS2 bilayers</p>\n                            <p><span>Article</span> <span><time datetime=\"2026-09-23\">23 SEP 26</time></span></p>\n                        </a>\n                    </li>","sentences":[{"en":"Stacking-induced direct band gap in CVD-grown 1H MoS2 bilayers Article 23 SEP 26","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p>Stacking-induced direct band gap in CVD-grown 1H MoS2 bilayers</p>","sentences":[{"en":"Stacking-induced direct band gap in CVD-grown 1H MoS2 bilayers","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p><span>Article</span> <span><time datetime=\"2026-09-23\">23 SEP 26</time></span></p>","sentences":[{"en":"Article 23 SEP 26","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<li>\n                        <a href=\"https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-03001-6\" data-track=\"select_article\" data-track-action=\"view latest magazine article\" data-track-index=\"3\">\n                            \n                                <img src=\"https://images.nature.com/w140h79/magazine-assets/d41586-026-03001-6/d41586-026-03001-6_53753634.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">\n                            \n                            <p>There's a new form of boron — and it's really weird</p>\n                            <p><span>News</span> <span><time datetime=\"2026-09-23\">23 SEP 26</time></span></p>\n                        </a>\n                    </li>","sentences":[{"en":"There's a new form of boron — and it's really weird News 23 SEP 26","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p>There's a new form of boron — and it's really weird</p>","sentences":[{"en":"There's a new form of boron — and it's really weird","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p><span>News</span> <span><time datetime=\"2026-09-23\">23 SEP 26</time></span></p>","sentences":[{"en":"News 23 SEP 26","zh":null}]}],"translated":true,"content_html_zh":"<div class=\"page\" id=\"readability-page-1\"><div id=\"content\" data-container-type=\"article\" data-component=\"article-container\">\n            \n\n            \n\n            <article data-track-component=\"news\" lang=\"en\">\n                \n                <div>\n                    \n                        <div>\n    <header>\n        <div>\n            <ul data-test=\"article-identifier\">\n                \n                    <li data-test=\"article-category\">RESEARCH BRIEFINGS</li>\n                    <li>23 September 2026</li>\n                \n                \n            </ul>\n\n            \n\n            <div>\n                \n                <p>Non-uniformities in the layer of passivator molecules, which are used to fix defects and protect the surface of perovskite material in solar cells, can limit the durability of the resulting modules. Large modules treated instead with chemically stable lead carboxylate passivators were efficient, reliable and had a higher yield than did commercial silicon modules.</p>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n        \n    </header>\n\n    \n    \n    \n        \n            \n    \n\n        \n    \n</div>\n                    \n\n                    \n\n                    \n                        \n                        <p>This is a summary of: Xu, D. et al. Lead carboxylates passivation for metre-scale perovskite solar modules. Nature 657, 918–924 (2026).</p>\n   